LUNA_PROVENANCE.json records original paths, upstream source SHA-256, adapted
LF-normalized SHA-256 and modifications. Changes replace GUI-coupled imports,
remove Google's unused browser/CDP path, correct Bing IG/IID assignment and replace
annotation-only requests / UTC-only pytz use with standard-library shims.
The compatibility interface, bounded HTTP session and isolated worker integration
are original ObliviousMic additions. No Qt GUI, browser driver or model is bundled.

Some web engines contain upstream-published web-client constants/signatures. These
are retained with their source attribution; they are not user credentials, and
are not a guarantee of unlimited access or future service availability.
API providers require the user's own credentials. No private credentials, text,
recordings or personalized models are included.

